Third-party components with different terms
-------------------------------------------

sidecars/potrace_sidecar/
    Potrace is licensed under the GNU General Public License v3. It is
    therefore NEVER imported into this codebase: the sidecar is a standalone
    script executed as a separate process over a pipe, and every feature of
    LaserTrace Pro works without it (the trace falls back to the built-in
    contour engine, with an ENGINE_FALLBACK warning). Its own licence text is
    in sidecars/potrace_sidecar/LICENSE.

PyMuPDF
    Not used. It is AGPL, which would be viral across this codebase. PDF input
    goes through pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause) instead.

Runtime dependencies
    numpy (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV (Apache-2.0), scikit-image (BSD-3-Clause),
    SciPy (BSD-3-Clause), Shapely (BSD-3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU),
    ezdxf (MIT), pydantic (MIT), pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause).

    The desktop shell additionally uses PySide6, which is LGPL-3 / GPL. It is
    used as an unmodified shared library, so distributing the app under the
    LGPL terms is straightforward; the `lasertrace` core and CLI have no Qt
    dependency at all if you would rather avoid it entirely.

See docs/TECH_STACK.md for the full audit.
